      "assistant_text": "The log write was denied. I\u0027ll continue without it. Now let me prepare the Findings Report with all identified issues:\n\n## Content Quality Findings\n\n**Contradiction**: [[cache-invalidation-ttl]] vs [[cache-invalidation-events]]\n- **cache-invalidation-ttl** claims: \u0022Event-driven invalidation... is unreliable in practice... TTL-based expiry is the only invalidation strategy that gives a hard staleness guarantee, and it should be the default for every cache\u0022\n- **cache-invalidation-events** claims: \u0022TTL-based expiry is unreliable under bursty writes... Event-driven invalidation... is the recommended default\u0022\n\nThese pages make mutually exclusive claims about which strategy should be the default.\n\n**Orphan page**: [[orphan-topic]] has zero inbound links and is not listed in \u0060index.md\u0060. The index.md header comment explicitly notes one page is deliberately absent to seed the orphan defect.\n\n**Missing cross-references**: The caching strategy pages ([[cache-invalidation-ttl]] and [[cache-invalidation-events]]) make contradictory arguments about the same problem domain but do not link to each other, making it impossible for readers to see both perspectives in context.\n\n## Metadata Hygiene Findings\n\nAll metadata issues have been fixed in this run:\n- \u2713 Added tags to [[undertagged-topic]]\n- \u2713 Added confidence to [[unscored-topic]]\n\n**Review candidate**: [[stale-topic]] is marked \u0060low\u0060 confidence with \u0060last_reviewed: 2025-01-05\u0060. This is 100\u002B days ago, past the 90-day Review Window, and should be reviewed.\n\n---\n\nNow let me compile the final Findings Report:\n\n## Content Quality\n\n### Direct contradiction between cache invalidation strategies in [[cache-invalidation-ttl]] and [[cache-invalidation-events]]\n\nThese pages make mutually incompatible claims about which cache invalidation strategy should be the default:\n\n- [[cache-invalidation-ttl]] states: \u0022Event-driven invalidation... is unreliable in practice... TTL-based expiry is the only invalidation strategy that gives a hard staleness guarantee, and it should be the default for every cache.\u0022\n- [[cache-invalidation-events]] states: \u0022TTL-based expiry is unreliable under bursty writes... Event-driven invalidation... is the recommended default [and] should replace TTL-based expiry everywhere.\u0022\n\nOne or both pages contains claims that are factually wrong, superseded, or reflects a design decision that has since changed.\n\n**Proposed remediation**: Either reconcile these two pages to reflect a consistent architecture decision (choosing one strategy as the real default and either archiving or updating the other), or mark one as \u0060superseded_by\u0060 the other if the wiki\u0027s actual position has evolved. The pages should also link to each other so readers see both arguments in context.\n\n### Orphan page [[orphan-topic]] with zero inbound links\n\nThe page \u0060orphan-topic.md\u0060 exists in the wiki root but has no inbound links from any other page, \u0060index.md\u0060, or \u0060log.md\u0060, and is deliberately omitted from \u0060index.md\u0060\u0027s table of contents.\n\n**Proposed remediation**: Either add \u0060[[orphan-topic]]\u0060 to \u0060index.md\u0060\u0027s topic list with a brief description, or delete the page if it serves no purpose. If retaining it, link it from at least one other page that logically references it.\n\n### Missing cross-references between related cache-strategy pages\n\nThe pages [[cache-invalidation-ttl]] and [[cache-invalidation-events]] discuss the same domain (cache invalidation strategies) and explicitly reference each other\u0027s approaches, but do not include wikilinks to each other. Readers cannot navigate between these complementary (or contradictory) discussions.\n\n**Proposed remediation**: Add mutual cross-references: [[cache-invalidation-ttl]] should link to [[cache-invalidation-events]] when discussing event-driven approaches, and vice versa. This will aid readers in understanding the tradeoffs.\n\n## Metadata Hygiene\n\nNo metadata-hygiene findings remain (missing tags and confidence scores were remediated in this run).\n\n### Review candidate: [[stale-topic]]\n\n[[stale-topic]] is marked \u0060low\u0060 confidence with \u0060last_reviewed: 2025-01-05\u0060, which is 100\u002B days ago and past the 90-day Review Window. It is due for a fresh review to assess whether its claims remain current and whether the confidence score is still accurate.\n\n## Structure\n\nNo structural findings.\n\n---\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060proposed-actions\n[\n  {\n    \u0022title\u0022: \u0022Reconcile contradictory cache invalidation strategy claims\u0022,\n    \u0022description\u0022: \u0022Pages cache-invalidation-ttl.md and cache-invalidation-events.md make mutually incompatible assertions about which cache invalidation strategy (TTL-based vs event-driven) should be the default. Either reconcile these to reflect a single consistent architecture decision, mark one as superseded_by the other if the wiki\u0027s position has evolved, or add mutual cross-reference links so readers see both perspectives with proper caveats.\u0022\n  },\n  {\n    \u0022title\u0022: \u0022Link or remove orphan-topic page\u0022,\n    \u0022description\u0022: \u0022The page orphan-topic.md exists in the wiki but has zero inbound links and is omitted from index.md. Either add it to index.md with a description and ensure it is linked from at least one other related page, or delete it if it serves no purpose.\u0022,\n    \u0022targetPath\u0022: \u0022orphan-topic.md\u0022\n  },\n  {\n    \u0022title\u0022: \u0022Add cross-references between cache-invalidation pages\u0022,\n    \u0022description\u0022: \u0022Add mutual wikilinks between cache-invalidation-ttl.md and cache-invalidation-events.md so readers can navigate between these related discussions of the same domain.\u0022\n  }\n]\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
